\id OBA - Open English Translation—Readers’ Version (OET-RV) v0.2.5
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h Obadiah
\toc1 Obadiah
\toc2 Obadiah
\mt1 Obadiah
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 \add This is\add* the vision of Obadiah \add given\add* by the master Yahweh concerning the Edom region:
\s1 Coming punishment for Edom
\q1 We have heard from Yahweh and a messenger has been sent to the nations, \add telling them:\add*
\q1 Get everything ready then go into battle against Edom.
\m
\v 2 \add And Yahweh says to Edom:\add*
\q1 Listen,
\q1 I will make you into an insignificant nation.
\q1 You’ll become utterly despised.
\q1
\v 3 Your inner pride has deceived you,
\q2 you who live on the rocky cliffs,
\q2 with your homes up there so high.
\q1 You say to yourselves \add that\add*
\q2 no one can bring you down to the ground.
\q1
\v 4 If you go up high like an eagle,
\q1 even if your nest was up between the stars,
\q1 Yahweh declares that his command can bring you down from there.
\b
\q1
\v 5 If \add it was\add* thieves who came to destroy you in the night,
\q2 (and yes, you’re going to be destroyed)
\q1 they would only steal what they wanted.
\q1 Or if \add it was\add* grape-pickers who came to you,
\q1 \add at least\add* they’d leave behind the smaller grapes.
\q1
\v 6 How Esau’s \add descendants\add* will be looted.
\q1 Their hidden treasures will be found \add and taken\add*.
\q1
\v 7 Those who have treaties with you will force you to the border.
\q1 Those who talk about peace will deceive you.
\q1 Those who eat meals with you will set a trap for you.
\q1 You have no idea what’s about to hit you.
\b
\q1
\v 8 Yahweh will make a declaration on that day.
\q1 The wise \add people\add* of Edom will be destroyed.
\q1 Understanding will disappear from Esau’s hill.
\q1
\v 9 And you Teyman \add region\add*, your warriors will be shattered,
\q1 so that everyone from Esau’s hill country will be slaughtered.
\s1 The charges against Edom
\q1
\v 10 Because of your violence against your brother Jacob’s \add descendants\add*,
\q1 shame will overcome you,
\q1 and you’ll be destroyed forever.
\q1
\v 11 You \add just\add* stood and watched on that day when strangers carried away their wealth.
\q1 When foreigners entered their gates and took possession of Jerusalem, you wished it was you doing that.
\q1
\v 12 You shouldn’t have gloated over your cousins on the day of their misfortune.
\q1 And you shouldn’t have celebrated about the destruction of the people of Judah.
\q1 You shouldn’t have bragged in \add their\add* time of distress.
\q1
\v 13 You shouldn’t have gone into their city at the time of their calamity.
\q1 You shouldn’t have gloated—yes, you—over their misery in their time of disaster.
\q1 And you \add women\add* shouldn’t have grabbed their wealth on the day of their catastrophe.
\q1
\v 14 You shouldn’t have stood at the crossroads to kill those trying to escape,
\q1 And you shouldn’t have handed-over any survivors that you’d captured in \add their\add* time of trouble.
\s1 The punishment of nations
\q1
\v 15 For all the nations, Yahweh’s day is near,
\q1 Just as you’ve done, the same will be done to you.
\q1 Your actions will return onto your own head.
\q1
\v 16 Because just like how all you \add Israelites\add*\f + \fr 1:16 \ft It’s not actually clear from the Hebrew who ‘you all’ refers to, so the addition of ‘Israelites’ is clearly an interpretive decision and other translations might differ.\f* drank \add suffering\add* on my holy mountain,
\q2 all the nations will drink continually.
\q1 They will drink and swallow it down.
\q1 They’ll become as if they’d never \add even\add* existed.
\s1 Israel’s victory
\s4 Both kingdoms
\q1
\v 17 But on Mt. Zion, there’ll be deliverance,
\q2 and it will be holy,
\q1 Israel’s people will reclaim their possessions.
\q1
\v 18 Israel’s people will be a fire,
\q1 and Joseph’s descendants will be a flame.
\q1 None of Esau’s descendants will survive,
\q1 because Yahweh has spoken.
\b
\q1
\v 19 \add The people from\add* the Negev will take ownership of Esau’s mountain,
\q1 and \add the people from\add* the Shefelah will take ownership of the Philistines’ \add land\add*.
\q1 They will recapture the Ephraim and Samaritan countrysides,
\q1 and \add the people of\add* Benjamin will recapture Gilead.
\q1
\v 20 Israel’s exiles will take ownership of the Canaanites’ \add land\add* as far as Zarephath,
\q1 and the exiles from Jerusalem who are in Sefarad) will take ownership of the cities of the Negev.
\q1
\v 21 The rescuers will go up Mt. Zion to judge Esau’s mountain.
\q1 and Yahweh will be their king.
